WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.007
I have a new watch. It is terrible.

00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:16.013
What you're looking at here is what's commonly called

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:22.500
an M4 wristband or fitness band or some such thing. It is the cheapest and nastier smart

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.460
watch that small amounts of money can buy. This cost me two francs sixty, which is about

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:34.780
fifty percent more than this knockoff blue pill cost me. What you get for this very small

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:42.540
amount of money? Not much. Technically this is a BLE attached smart watch. It connects

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:48.380
to a mobile phone, a computer, notifications and things to it. Practically it's basically

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:55.020
trash. They achieve the price point by cutting out all the extraneous features like battery

00:00:55.020 --> 00:01:02.100
life and reliability and a user interface and buttons and stuff like that. Let me take

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:10.020
it off my wrist and I'll give you the tour. The silicone wristband came with it. The watch

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:18.940
itself just pops out like that. This is the first watch face. This one is built in. You

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:24.380
get a choice of two, one of which is programmable from the smartphone app. Pressing the button

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:34.500
cycles you through the main menu. A long press selects the item. So the steps function

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:41.140
is a step counter. That while I have been playing with this on my desk has gone up by about

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:50.180
two hundred. So I am not convinced that is like accurate, maybe real. Heart rate is the

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:56.980
heart rate sensor. It also somehow detects blood pressure and blood oxygen levels. It works

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:05.260
by blinking the LED on the bottom for a long period of time. And then eventually it comes

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:13.820
up with a number which is always about this. I don't think the heart sensor is real.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:21.740
The watch is a bunch of sport related activities. We've got running, skipping and sit up. These

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:31.220
are all the same. If I select it, it seems to be a timer. It may hook up to the step counter

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:36.020
to make the K-Cal thing work. Assuming that's real. Let me just shake this about a bit.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:46.180
Has it done anything? No. So moving on. Message. This is possibly the only actual useful feature

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:51.900
the thing has. This allows your smartphone to push messages to the watch and it displays

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.460
them on the screen. I currently don't have it hooked up to the phones which just says

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:03.260
null and if I select it, nothing happens. Sleep appears to be some kind of sleep sensor.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:09.780
I don't know how this works and I don't care. Weather pulls weather information from an

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:15.820
unknown source on the smartphone app. No smartphone. Therefore it says it is sunny and zero

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:26.220
degrees. Music lets you control your phone's music player. Somehow it is deeply cumbersome.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:31.820
A single press cycles the cursor. A long press actually makes the thing happen. Of course

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:40.220
no smartphone so it doesn't do anything. More takes you to more items. First on of which

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:45.460
is the camera. This does not have a camera. What this does is triggers the camera on your

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:53.740
phone. Again, no smartphone doesn't do anything. Looking for causes the smartphone to vibrate

00:03:53.740 --> 00:04:00.260
and the phone has an equivalent feature that causes the wristband to vibrate. This could

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:06.740
actually be useful. These things are so cheap that you could use one as a locator. Buy

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:13.060
it, stick it on a keychain somewhere, except the battery life is not brilliant. I'll talk

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:18.140
about that later. Theme lets you switch between the two watch faces. You've got the built-in

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:23.940
one. Programmerable one. The smartphone app lets you program this to a limited extent.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:29.900
You can basically just change the backdrop. I've used a completely black one here and you

