01:07:37.540 --> 01:07:46.900
value we multiply it by 4. We load the address of the jump table. We add the jump table address to

01:07:46.900 --> 01:07:54.500
the multiply by 4 value. Read the address and jump. But these are not addresses. These are bytes.

01:07:55.620 --> 01:08:03.300
This just doesn't work. It's garbage. Luckily there's a compiler flag that allows you to make the

01:08:03.300 --> 01:08:11.860
